        "category": "error-handling",
        "title": "get_fields_from_path can raise for non-field related attributes",
        "explanation": "The getattr traversal succeeds for any attribute, including properties on the related model (e.g. parent__some_property). get_fields_from_path only resolves real model fields, so it raises FieldDoesNotExist or NotRelationField. lookup_field previously returned f=None in that case and the changelist rendered normally. Now it can crash the changelist.",
        "suggestion": "Wrap the call in try/except (FieldDoesNotExist, NotRelationField) and leave f as None on failure.",
        "evidence": "f = get_fields_from_path(opts.model, name)[-1]",
        "confidence": 0.5,
